An application for a business license to operate as a professional bondsman in the city shall be accompanied by written approval of the chief of police, who shall investigate the applicant and issue such approval when he finds that the applicant is:
(1) Eighteen (18) years of age or over;
(2) A resident of the State of Georgia for at least one (1) year before making application to write bonds;
(3) A person of good moral character and has not been convicted of a felony or any crime involving moral turpitude; and
(4) Approved by the sheriff of Cobb County, Georgia, and remains in good standing with respect to all applicable federal, state and local laws and all rules and regulations established by the city and the Cobb County, Georgia, sheriff.
(Ord. No. 96-17, 8-19-96)

